{%- comment -%}
  Skip link
  WCAG 2.4.1 Bypass Blocks (Level A)

  Render as the first element inside <body> in layout/theme.liquid:

    {% render 'a11y-skip-link' %}

  The target must exist and must be focusable. In theme.liquid:

    <main id="MainContent" role="main" tabindex="-1">

  tabindex="-1" is the part that is usually missing. Without it several
  browsers scroll to the target but leave focus where it was, so the next Tab
  press returns to the second navigation link and the skip link has done
  nothing. The bug is invisible unless you press Tab straight after activating
  the link.

  Do not hide this with display:none or visibility:hidden. Both remove it from
  the tab order, so it can never be reached and never used. It must be offset
  off screen while remaining focusable.
{%- endcomment -%}

<a class="a11y-skip-link" href="#MainContent">
  {{ 'accessibility.skip_to_text' | t: default: 'Skip to main content' }}
</a>

{%- style -%}
  .a11y-skip-link {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    z-index: 1000;
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    background: rgb(var(--color-background, 255 255 255));
    color: rgb(var(--color-foreground, 18 18 18));
    text-decoration: underline;
    transform: translateY(-200%);
  }

  .a11y-skip-link:focus {
    transform: translateY(0);
    outline: 3px solid rgb(var(--color-foreground, 18 18 18));
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
{%- endstyle -%}
